window.docContents[107].resolve({"/Solver/#Cvc___lean----High-Level-API-for-CVC5--Solver--Basics":{"contents":"A solver instance.\n\nSolver creation and virtually all solver functions run in the Env monad.Some run in\nstronger monads than Env, as we will see very soon.\n\nCreates a new solver.\n\nSome functions such as setLogic are actually defined on Untyped.Solver, but since Typed.Solver\nis just an alias for the untyped version we can use them on both types.\n\nSet logic.* logic: The logic to set.\n\nSet option.* option: The option name.* value: The option value.\n\nSetting options also has a typed version that takes a Solver.Option, an enumeration of most\nof cvc5's options, and a value of the appropriate type for that option.\n\nSets an option in a solver.\n\n#eval Env.runIO do\n  let solver ← Solver.new\n  solver.setLogic .qf_lia\n  solver.setOption \"produce-models\" \"true\"\n  solver.setOpt .smt_produceUnsatCores true\n  println! \"logic: {← solver.getLogic}\"\n  let val ← solver.getOption \"produce-models\"\n  println! \"produce-models: {val}\"\n\n\nWhile it is possible to declare function symbols in a solver, it is strictly equivalent to creating\na solver-agnostic symbol with Term.mkSymbol/Term.mkSymbolAs. Both simply create a new symbol in\nthe underlying term manager.\n\n#eval Env.runIO do\n  let b ← Term.mkSymbol \"b\"\n  let solver ← Solver.new\n  let i ← solver.declareConst \"i\"\n  let f ← Term.mkSymbolAs (Bool → Int → Int) \"f\"\n  let g ← solver.declareFunAs (Int → Int → Int) \"g\"\n\n  let t ← smt! 0 ≤ g (f b i) i\n  solver.assert t\n  solver.assert b\n  println! \"assertions:\"\n  for a in ← solver.getAssertions do\n    -- note that `a : Term Bool`\n    println! \"- {a}\"\n\n\nassertions:\n- (<= 0 (g (f b i) i))\n- b\n\n\nAs shown above Solver.assert adds a Term Bool assertion in the solver.\n\nAssert a formula.* term: The formula to assert.\n\n","context":"Cvc.lean -- High-Level API for CVC5\u0009Solver","header":"6.1. Basics","id":"/Solver/#Cvc___lean----High-Level-API-for-CVC5--Solver--Basics"}});